WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.879
This example uses CASE inside an aggregate For each
admission the

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:11.118
CASE expression asks whether the diagnosis matches a
condition A matching row

00:00:11.145 --> 00:00:15.355
contributes a value such as one and a non-matching
row contributes zero

00:00:16.289 --> 00:00:21.810
SUM then adds those contributions inside each
patient group Run the

00:00:21.837 --> 00:00:27.386
query and inspect the separate pneumonia and
fracture counts Before

00:00:27.413 --> 00:00:30.597
running it choose one patient from the data and
predict the two

00:00:30.623 --> 00:00:36.546
counts Then compare your prediction with the result
This

00:00:36.573 --> 00:00:41.549
pattern is flexible because CASE can handle more
than simple equality You

00:00:41.575 --> 00:00:46.207
can build conditions based on ranges multiple
columns or more complex business

00:00:46.233 --> 00:00:51.675
rules When using CASE for counting make sure the
values you return

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:53.885
are appropriate for the aggregate you apply
